  "notes": "Smoke-only BLE runtime resource cleanup. Replaces the single deferred-client pointer with a bounded deduplicated reclamation queue, reuses static NimBLE callbacks to reduce heap fragmentation, and clears volatile scan, handshake, diagnostics, and session state without erasing BLE bonds or user settings. Adds free-heap and largest-block monitoring with a safe BLE-stack recycle only after persistent memory pressure while disconnected and idle; active generation, mode selection, OTA, and working phone/Twin links are never interrupted. The persistent diagnostics cache is now capped at 48 KiB during runtime, writes events in batches, retains the newest queued records, and rate-limits routine scan/heap telemetry to reduce SPIFFS stalls that could disturb LED and button timing. The proven manual power-off path still avoids deinitializing a live BLE connection. Twin Button firmware content remains unchanged.",
